{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["By the hand of YHWH — the death of those who come to the grave by the sword, and not by famine." "By the flesh-pot — like: ועליו מטה מנשה."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The parenthetical הבאים בכלח appears to be a biblical quotation (cf. Psalm 63:10, יבאים בכלח); the word אלי may be a variant or scribal form for אל (unto). The verse reference is not given in the source.", 1 "Comparison to Joshua 17:1, where על with the accusative means 'over' or 'at' — i.e., they sat 'at' the flesh-pot."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:42.974501845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}